ected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026 because power availability is limiting them.\n  - Demand is still rising, so the thesis holds.\n- **Financing: a real risk to the capex plans.**\n  - Debt markets are open, but utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n  - Equity is largely shut. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short, and scaled back procurement.\n  - The full 2027 plans can't be funded as written, so some orders may slip or shrink. The evidence here is thin.\n- **Pricing: fair, not cheap.**\n  - VLTX LEAPS implied volatility is 27%, against a 2-year median of 26%.\n  - There is no pricing edge to justify adding.\n  - The only evidence on price was a short snapshot and a three-point implied-vol series. It didn't include the VLTX stock price or strikes, so I haven't assessed those.\n\nDemand is positive, financing is a risk, and the options aren't cheap. That doesn't make a case for adding now.\n\nI'd reconsider if one of these changes:\n- Implied vol falls well below its median.\n- Utility equity or debt financing improves.\n- Order or procurement news confirms the 2027 capex plans are intact.\n\nThe full reasoning is in the three sub-analyses: n2.r1 (demand), n3.r1 (financing) and n4.r1 (pricing).","ttft_ms":2021,"type":"result","duration_ms":37068,"uuid":"39be549f-4f97-4685-85e8-99773e2a2ff8","ttft_stream_ms":1193,"time_to_request_ms":202,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":34,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":25,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":12,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":28,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":4,"tool_schema_build":8,"message_normalization":8,"client_creation":16,"request_build":17},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":140,"time_t